4.
TY  - WEB
AB  - This draft political declaration addresses the increasing proportion of civilian casualties in contemporary, urbanized conflicts due to the use of explosive weapons in populated areas. It highlights the devastating immediate and long-term reverberating effects on civilians and critical infrastructure, emphasizing the need for full compliance with International Humanitarian Law (IHL) and International Human Rights Law. The declaration commits signatories to strengthening the protection of civilians by improving national policies, providing comprehensive training for armed forces, restricting the use of explosive weapons with wide area effects, and enhancing international cooperation. It also emphasizes the importance of data collection on civilian casualties, victim assistance, and unimpeded humanitarian access.
