7.
TY  - WEB
AB  - This statement by the Netherlands at the Geneva Consultation on Protecting Civilians in Urban Warfare emphasizes the importance of adhering to existing International Humanitarian Law (IHL) and International Human Rights Law (IHRL). The Netherlands expresses concern over the growing threat to civilians from both state and non-state actors, particularly the use of Improvised Explosive Devices (IEDs). The statement advocates for full and universal respect for IHL principles and warns against selectively focusing on specific IHL rules, which could undermine the overall legal framework. The Netherlands also supports a political declaration to improve IHL compliance, outlining key elements such as binding IHL requirements, respect for existing IHL, and enhanced transparency in data collection on civilian harm.
