8.
TY  - WEB
AB  - This statement, delivered on behalf of 21 UN and other humanitarian organizations at the Geneva Consultations on November 18, 2019, addresses the catastrophic humanitarian impact of urban warfare, particularly the use of explosive weapons in populated areas. It welcomes the initiation of work on a political declaration to mitigate the devastating effects of such weapons, emphasizing the need to recognize both direct and reverberating consequences. The statement advocates for commitments to avoid the use of explosive weapons with wide-area effects and to improve military practices, data collection, and victim assistance. Ultimately, the goal is a declaration that significantly reduces harm to civilians in urban conflicts.
