10.
TY  - WEB
AB  - This paper explores the use of Bayesian Networks and Influence Diagrams to aid decision-making in asymmetric urban warfare scenarios. These probabilistic techniques help determine the most probable outcomes based on available intelligence, assisting commanders in estimating the timing and location of potential attacks. The methodology is robust to changes in data, but the time required for development limits real-time applicability. These tools are most useful during intelligence preparation and as decision support for troop allocation and operational planning.
